# Daily technical analysis run for the finance pipeline.
#
# The schedule is unchanged from the original deployment: 18:10 on
# weekdays, after the Tokyo close at 15:00. It is kept as it is because
# it works and the operator relies on it, and there is no reason to
# prefer a systemd timer for a plain daily batch.
#
# The hour matters less than it once did. The data source publishes in
# arrears, so a run collects what was published long before it and an
# occasional missed evening costs nothing the next run does not pick up.
#
# The job needs the J-Quants API key, which run.sh reads from the
# environment file in the deployment root. It is deliberately not set
# here: /etc/cron.d is world readable.
#
# run.sh exits non-zero when a step fails, so cron mails root on a
# partial run instead of the failure going unnoticed.

SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin

10 18  * * 1-5 root test -x /var/stock/run.sh && /var/stock/run.sh
